    "assumptions": [
      "Unmeasured internal construction is solid. The grip core is steel; hidden cavities, tangs, fasteners and alloys are unknown. No thickness or density is calibrated to the museum mass.",
      "The museum identifies steel, silver wire and a silver pommel. The lower button is included with the silver pommel; all other fittings are represented as steel. Silver uses elemental density 10500 kg/m3, not an identified historical alloy.",
      "The beak has a transverse diamond section whose two diagonals remain equal while tapering. This follows the catalog description of a square section; the photographs alone do not measure its hidden depth.",
